  "summary": "Four recent preprints target practical limits on structured optical fields, from turbulent transmission to reconstruction cost and measurement noise.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is maintaining the fidelity of optical field information under practical limits such as turbulence, quantization, and measurement noise. Active convolved illumination is reviewed as a framework for preserving optical mode structure through turbulent media via segmented reciprocal-space control. In binary-encoded Fourier single-pixel imaging, a Fourier-domain response-matrix correction addresses quantization errors. A cross-harmonic neural network uses first and second harmonic nano-FTIR signals to denoise third-harmonic hyperspectral data on a PMMA/PS sample. Stochastic gradient descent is proposed for X-ray ptychographic reconstruction, reducing peak GPU memory and computation time. The items do not share a single method; they differ in modality and mechanism. What is new is the targeted application of mode preservation, error correction, and computational denoising or reconstruction to specific imaging tasks.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
